 ],
 "literal": "Fragrant white hair that has abandoned pleasant speech / wrinkled-nippled empty breasts like dark heartwood / the beloved young son of the noble old woman / like a few drops of curd flicked by the sharp fingernail of an innocent cowherd woman / into a pot of milk / he himself became the entire destruction to the enemy army.",
 "translation": "The beloved young son of the noble old woman—who has fragrant white hair, who no longer speaks sweet words, and whose empty breasts with wrinkled nipples are strong like dark heartwood—became himself the sole destruction of the entire enemy army, just like a few drops of curd flicked from the sharp fingernail of an innocent cowherd woman that curdles a whole pot of milk.",
 "modern": "இனிய சொற்களைப் பேசுவதை விடுத்த, நறுமணமுள்ள நரைத்த கூந்தலையும், இருண்ட மரவைரம் போன்ற சுருங்கிய காம்புகளைக் கொண்ட வற்றிய முலைகளையும் உடைய சிறந்த முதிய தாயின் அன்பிற்குரிய சிறுமகன், இளமையான ஆயர் மகள் தன் கூர்மையான நகத்தால் தெறித்துவிட்ட சில துளிகள் உறைமோர் ஒரு குடம் பால் முழுவதையும் தயிராக்குவது போல, பகைவர் படை முழுவதற்கும் தானே அழிவாக மாறினான்.",
 "explanation": "This poem belongs to the tumpai tiṇai (warfare) and the tāṉainilai theme, which describes the heroic stand of a warrior in battle. The poet praises a young hero by first describing his mother, a noble old woman with gray hair and empty, wrinkled breasts that are as tough as dark heartwood. This description highlights the strength and resilience of the mother who raised such a brave warrior. The central focus of the poem is a brilliant simile comparing the warrior's impact on the enemy to a cowherd woman curdling milk. Just as a tiny drop of sour curd flicked from a fingernail transforms and curdles an entire pot of milk, this single young hero enters the massive enemy army and completely destroys its order and strength. The key words are 'cemmutu peṇṭiṉ' (noble old woman), 'cilluṟai' (few drops of curd), and 'paṭaikkunōy' (destruction to the army).",
